      "html": "<h3>Can Quickler use my own report template?</h3><p>Yes, and this is the main difference from other inspection software. Upload the finished report your firm already sends to clients, in Word or PDF, or even a photograph of one. Every record comes back inside that document with your styles, headings, tables, headers, footer and logo preserved. Quickler reads a finished report rather than a blank form, so it can separate your firm's standing wording from one visit's facts and place each record's words where yours were. Other tools give you their layout and you rebuild yours at the desk afterwards.</p><h3>How much does Quickler cost?</h3><p>£50 per active user per month, with a £50 monthly minimum. An active user is someone who completed at least one check that month; everyone else is free, so you add your whole team and pay only for the people who actually worked. A 30-person team with 5 regular inspectors pays £250 a month, against £570 to £720 on per-seat pricing at £19 to £24 a seat. There is a free tier of 20 reports a month, up to 10 photos per report, free forever with no card and no trial clock. Billed monthly in arrears by UK Direct Debit, no setup fee.</p><h3>Is Quickler cheaper than iAuditor or SafetyCulture?</h3><p>It depends on the shape of your team, and we will be straight about it. Per-seat tools charge for every person on the licence whether they inspect daily or never open the app, so Quickler is substantially cheaper wherever a whole team needs access but only a handful do the walking: a care home, a school estate, a cleaning firm. If nearly everyone on your team inspects most days, for example five people all doing daily checks, a per-seat app will be cheaper than us.</p><h3>Does my team need to install an app?</h3><p>No. They answer in the WhatsApp already on their phone, or Telegram if you prefer, chosen per person. There is no app to install, no login to remember and no training. The usual reason inspection software quietly fails is that the people on site stop opening the app; Quickler removes that failure mode entirely. Only the manager signs in to the dashboard, with a magic link, a six-digit code or a passkey.</p><h3>Does Quickler make things up or guess answers?</h3><p>No, and this is enforced rather than hoped for. Every name, number and identifier written on a record has to stand in something actually said, sent or photographed. Where two answers disagree, or a date reads two ways, Quickler raises it for a person to settle, quoting the words it heard and when they were said, rather than quietly choosing one. A plan to fix something is kept as a note, never recorded as the answer. A record never files itself just because every question happens to have been answered: somebody says done, or it waits.</p><h3>Is Quickler a care records system or an eMAR?</h3><p>No. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer, not a clinical or care records system. It does not hold care plans, medication rounds, resident records or rostering, and those stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. It records that a check was done and keeps the evidence with it. It is also not job management software: no scheduling of work, no invoicing, no dispatch.</p>"
